  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Harira is thickened at the end with a flour-water paste called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "tedouira ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "tedouira"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The distinctive flavour also comes from the cooked-in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "herb base",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "charmoula-herb-base"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " of coriander and celery that goes in at the start. A generous squeeze of lemon at the table is the finishing touch."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If using dried chickpeas, soak overnight and cook separately before adding. Tinned chickpeas save 2 hours and work just as well here."
          }
        ]
      },
